\text { Finkelstein reaction }
$$

When an alkene is heated with $\mathrm{Cl}_2$ at high temperature, hydrogen atom of allylic carbon is substituted with halogen atom giving allyl halide.
$$
\begin{gathered}
\mathrm{CH}_2=\mathrm{CH}-\mathrm{CH}_3+\mathrm{Cl}_2 \longrightarrow \\
\mathrm{CH}_2=\mathrm{CH}-\mathrm{CH}_2 \mathrm{Cl}+\mathrm{HCl} \\
\text { 3-Chloropropene }
\end{gathered}
$$

